{% doc %}
  SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for how many items each paginated template shows per page.
  Outputs a bare integer. Consumed by:

    sections/ona-blog-news-template.liquid   (Journal)
    sections/ona-blog-template.liquid        (Brew Guides + any other blog)
    sections/ona-collection-template.liquid
    sections/ona-search-results.liquid
    snippets/meta-robots-pagination.liquid   (layout/<head>)

  Why it exists: the robots snippet runs in the layout, where `paginate` is not in
  scope, so it has to recompute the page count from the item total and the page
  size. When that page size was duplicated by hand, lowering a section's limit
  without updating the snippet would have made the snippet compute FEWER pages
  than really exist and noindex real, populated pages. Reading both numbers from
  here makes that drift impossible.

  To change a page size, change it HERE and nowhere else.

  Usage in a section (capture yields a string, so coerce it back to a number):
    {%- capture limit -%}{%- render 'paginate-page-size' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign limit = limit | strip | plus: 0 -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign page_size = 24
  if template.name == 'blog' and blog.handle == 'news'
    assign page_size = 12
  endif
  echo page_size
-%}
